  "raw": " usual amount, according to a study by PwC published Monday.\n\nOther countries' responses provided some of the world's biggest contrasts to U.S. participation: Only 40% of Canadian fathers claimed any time off during new fatherhood. Britain's slowing birth rate could lead to additional unpaid work, shortages of care workers or an increase in unplanned pregnancies among parents who want merely to focus on child-rearing, research suggests. The Netherlands has implemented several programs designed largely around mothers' needs.\n\nYoung men, especially, should know they are considered valued members of society, say researchers. Though there are indeed societal expectations for new fathers to reduce their workload prior to parenthood, men can build trust and instill hope throughout child development simply by being present,\" PwC US Federal Leaders Paternity Research Report says. It is important for communities, companies and individuals to provide fathers with postpartum supports, including through parental/dependent leave policies.\"",
  "serialized": "usual amount, according to a study by PwC published Monday. Other countries' responses provided some of the world's biggest contrasts to U.S. participation: Only 40% of Canadian fathers claimed any time off during new fatherhood. Britain's slowing birth rate could lead to additional unpaid work, shortages of care workers or an increase in unplanned pregnancies among parents who want merely to focus on child-rearing, research suggests. The Netherlands has implemented several programs designed largely around mothers' needs. Young men, especially, should know they are considered valued members of society, say researchers. Though there are indeed societal expectations for new fathers to reduce their workload prior to parenthood, men can build trust and instill hope throughout child development simply by being present,\" PwC US Federal Leaders Paternity Research Report says. It is important for communities, companies and individuals to provide fathers with postpartum supports, including through parental/dependent leave policies.\"",
